{"id":"~Aikys_Mongush1","name":"Aikys Mongush","counts":{"accepted_papers":1,"first_position_papers":0,"co_first_author_papers":null,"corresponding_author_papers":null,"Oral":1},"papers":[{"id":"5XKFwWrW0v","title":"π0.7: a Steerable Generalist Robotic Foundation Model with Emergent Capabilities","abstract":"We present a new robotic foundation model, called $\\pi_{0.7}$, that can enable strong out-of-the-box performance in a wide range of scenarios. The main idea behind $\\pi_{0.7}$ is to use diverse context conditioning during training. This conditioning information, contained in the prompt, makes it possible to steer the model precisely to perform many tasks with different strategies. \nIt is conditioned not just on a language command that describes what it should do, but on additional multimodal information that also describes the manner or strategy in which it should do it, including metadata about task performance and subgoal images. This enables $\\pi_{0.7}$ to use very diverse data, including demonstrations, potentially suboptimal (autonomous) data including failures, and data from non-robot sources. Our experiments evaluate $\\pi_{0.7}$ across numerous tasks that require speed and dexterity, language following, and compositional task generalization.","summary":"以更丰富的上下文条件控制通用机器人基础模型，整合示范与自主数据，探索可引导的执行策略、精细技能和新任务泛化。论文为公司团队署名，个人作者顺序需结合其署名方式理解。","type":"Oral","topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型","模仿与示范学习","灵巧操作与机器人手","安全、泛化与鲁棒性"],"title_topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型"],"authors":["~Bo_Ai1","~Ali_Amin2","~Raichelle_Aniceto1","~Ashwin_Balakrishna1","~Greg_Balke1","~Kevin_Black2","~George_Elledge_Bokinsky1","~Shihao_Cao1","~Thomas_Charbonnier1","~Vedant_Choudhary2","~Foster_Collins2","~Ken_Conley1","~Grace_B_Connors1","~James_Darpinian1","~Karan_Dhabalia1","~Maitrayee_Dhaka1","~Jared_Di_Carlo1","~Danny_Driess1","~Michael_Robert_Equi1","~Adnan_Esmail1","~Yunhao_Fang1","~Chelsea_Finn1","~Catherine_Glossop1","~Thomas_Godden1","~Ivan_Goryachev1","~Lachy_Groom1","~Haroun_Habeeb2","~Hunter_H